      "side": 1,
      "message": "Prefer `this.patchNum` (when not `EDIT`) over `this.latestPatchNum` when loading revision actions.\n\nBecause `this.latestPatchNum` is populated by `ChangeModel` as soon as the change loads, `this.latestPatchNum ?? this.patchNum` always evaluates to `this.latestPatchNum` in production and ignores `this.patchNum` when viewing or switching between earlier patchsets (the unit test `loads revision actions and hides Agent Chat when aiReview is disabled` only hits the fallback because `element.latestPatchNum` is `undefined` in that test). In addition:\n1. When navigating directly to a non-latest patchset diff URL, `this.patchNum` is available from the route before `this.latestPatchNum` is populated, so `loadRevisionActions()` fetches actions for `this.patchNum` first and then immediately refetches for `this.latestPatchNum` once the change loads.\n2. When opening a diff in edit mode (`this.patchNum \u003d\u003d\u003d EDIT`) before `this.latestPatchNum` is populated, `patchNum` resolves to `\u0027edit\u0027`, which is not a valid revision ID for `GET /changes/{id}/revisions/{revision-id}/actions`.\n\n```suggestion\n  private async loadRevisionActions() {\n    const patchNum \u003d\n      this.patchNum \u0026\u0026 this.patchNum !\u003d\u003d EDIT\n        ? this.patchNum\n        : this.latestPatchNum;\n    if (!this.changeNum || !patchNum) {\n      return;\n    }\n```",
